@using static FellowshipAnalyzer.Core.Analysis.Changelog
@using static FellowshipAnalyzer.Core.Analysis.Contributors

@code {
    public static readonly IReadOnlyList<ChangelogEntry> Entries =
    [
        Change(new(2026, 7, 28), @<text>Rewrote every guide around what good play looks like rather than how the ability works. Culling Strike is now rated on converting the cooldown: every charge the execute phase offered, split into presses on cooldown, holds with Fury banked, and holds while Fury was short. This needed a fix in the spellbook - the five abilities S3 marks <c>SpellCDHasted</c> were not flagged as hasted, so their cooldowns were modelled at the unhasted duration. Executioner's Grin now hangs off the bands being equipped and separates procs spent above the threshold, which is what the item buys, from procs spent on a cast that was already legal and procs that expired with no cast at all. Hammer Storm states its break-even: it returns 0.61x a Skull Crusher per point of Fury on one target and 1.18x on two, so single-target channels are marked. Leap Smash is out of the Fury economy entirely - it is a movement cooldown, and charging its gain as waste framed pressing it as a cost. Major Cooldowns is split into separate Empowerment Windows and Focused Wrath sections.</text>, Seriousnes),
        Change(new(2026, 7, 28), @<text>Validated every premise against a live log and cut the ones it refused to confirm. Culling Strike's execute coverage percentage is gone - its cooldown is hasted and was observed as low as 1.5s, so there is no honest count of casts a phase "had room for"; the phase now reports casts landed, duration, and the health each cast went out at, with Executioner's Grin recorded per cast. Focused Wrath is measured per buff rather than per cast, because Leap Smash procs the same buff and grants five times as many as the cooldown does. Hammer Storm no longer grades channels against a three-target threshold that is not in the game data. Fury discipline's share-of-potential percentage is gone, since auto-attacks and Hammer Storm's passive trickle are not in the denominator. Rising Spirit no longer clamps its stack count at five, and Skull Crusher's Sledgehammer splash is attributed to it.</text>, Seriousnes),
        Change(new(2026, 7, 26), @<text>Season 3 rebuild: corrected the talent registry for the rework, added Fury tracking as a percentage of the stat-scaled pool, rewrote Fury economy on points-based overcap waste, and added Major Cooldowns (Thunder Call windows and Focused Wrath pairing), Hammer Storm channel and Schism proc analysis, Culling Strike execute coverage, and a Rising Spirit statistic.</text>, Seriousnes),
        Change(new(2026, 7, 12), @<text>Added the spellbook, and Culling Strike execute usage now accounts for Executioner's Grin (the item proc that lets it be used above 30% health).</text>, Seriousnes),
        Change(new(2026, 7, 10), @<text>Pull-scoped Fury economy analysis and guide.</text>, Seriousnes),
    ];
}
